<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">health</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">Health</ansi> (HP) represents how much physical punishment
your character can endure. Your maximum Health is based
primarily on your Vitality stat.

Health will change color to reflect your condition:

<ansi fg="health-100">100%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-90">90%-99%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-80">80%-89%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-70">70%-79%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-60">60%-69%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-50">50%-59%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-40">40%-49%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-30">30%-39%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-20">20%-29%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-10">10%-19%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-0">0%-9%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-dead">dead</ansi>

When your Health drops to zero, you collapse and begin
bleeding out. If you are not aided in time, you will die --
but death on Gaius does not delete your character. You wake
at your home point, weakened by the brush with death, and
your gear stays with you. See <ansi fg="command">help death</ansi> for what a
fall truly costs and how to avoid paying it.

Health regenerates slowly over time, recovering faster
when you are out of combat. Certain spells and items can
speed the healing process.

